# Profiler output is machine-generated, machine-specific, and regenerable, so it does not belong
# in git. The binary captures were always excluded; the text dumps of the same runs were tracked
# anyway, which was the same rule applied twice in opposite directions.
#
# The exception is the one that earns it: a capture a write-up NAMES is the evidence for a number
# it quotes, and deleting it turns that number into an unverifiable claim (library-standards C1).
# Those are force-added -- see the list below, and add to it when a vN.md starts citing a file.
*.ncu-rep
*.nsys-rep
*.sqlite
*.ncu.log
ncu.status
*.txt
*.csv

# cited by the write-up beside them
!triangle_multiplication_tm1_cute/v1/nsys_kern_L1024_cuda_gpu_kern_sum.csv
!triangle_multiplication_tm1_cute/v2/nsys_kern_L1024_cuda_gpu_kern_sum.csv
!triangle_multiplication_tm1_cute/v8/nsys_kern_L1024_cuda_gpu_kern_sum.csv
!triangle_multiplication_tm1_cute/v9/ncu_gk_occupancy.txt
!trimul_cuequiv_free_b200/v1/nsys_kern_sum.txt
